        "original_id": "5014e3ae-55d9-5d24-a275-47018b9b4f87",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Topics: Southern United States cuisine, American cuisine\n- Concepts: meat and three, chicken fried steak, country fried steak\n- Foods: fried chicken, country ham, beef, meatloaf, pork chop, vegetables, potatoes, corn, green beans, lima beans, gelatin, creamed corn, macaroni and cheese, spaghetti\n\nFacts:\n- In Southern United States cuisine, a meat and three restaurant lets a customer choose one meat from a daily selection of three to six options.\n- In Southern United States cuisine, the meat options at a meat and three restaurant can include fried chicken, country ham, beef, country-fried steak, meatloaf, or pork chop.\n- In Southern United States cuisine, a meat and three restaurant also lets a customer choose three side dishes from a list that may include up to about a dozen options.\n- In Southern United States cuisine, the side dishes at a meat and three restaurant usually include vegetables, potatoes, corn, green beans, or lima beans, and can also include gelatin, creamed corn, macaroni and cheese, or spaghetti.\n- In American cuisine, chicken fried steak, also called country fried steak, is a breaded cutlet dish.\n- In American cuisine, chicken fried steak consists of a piece of steak, specifically tenderized cube steak, coated with seasoned flour and pan-fried.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
